  <p class="identity"><span>Hustle Street</span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><span>Privacy Policy</span></p>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="meta">Last updated: 10 November 2026</p>

  <p>This policy explains what happens to information when you play <strong>Hustle Street</strong> on iPhone, iPad or Android. It is written for players aged 10 and up and for their parents.</p>
  <p>Hustle Street is published by <strong>Abren Systems LLC</strong>, a company registered in New Mexico, United States (“we”, “us”). If you have any question, email us at <a href="mailto:support@abrensystems.com">support@abrensystems.com</a>.</p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>There are no accounts, no sign-up and no login.</li>
    <li>The game shows no ads, uses no advertising IDs, and does not track you across other apps or websites.</li>
    <li>Your saved games and progress stay on your phone or tablet. We never receive them.</li>
    <li>The game sends anonymous game statistics that identify no one. You can turn them off in Settings.</li>
    <li>We don’t sell or share personal data.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>1. No accounts, no ads, no ad tracking</h2>
  <p>You don’t need to sign up or log in to play. The game shows no ads, uses no advertising IDs, and does not track players across other apps or websites. We don’t sell or share personal data.</p>

  <h2>2. Your game data stays on your device</h2>
  <p>Saved games, your street, profile names you type in the game, your settings and your progress are stored only on your phone or tablet. We never receive them. If you delete the app, they are deleted too.</p>

  <h2>3. Anonymous game statistics</h2>
  <p>To learn how the game is played and make it better, the app sends anonymous gameplay events. For example: a game started or finished, the game mode and how long it lasted, a tip being shown, the first time the app is opened, whether it was opened again one day and seven days later, and which new game features were viewed.</p>
  <p>These events:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>identify no one.</strong> They contain no name, email, contact details, location, advertising ID or any other identifier that follows a person. Each time the app is launched it uses a new random code, which is never stored.</li>
    <li><strong>are processed by our analytics provider, PostHog,</strong> on servers in the United States. IP addresses are discarded and not stored. See <a href="https://posthog.com/privacy">PostHog’s privacy policy</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>can be turned off at any time</strong> in the game’s Settings with “Share anonymous game stats”. This setting is on when you first install the game.</li>
    <li><strong>are kept for 12 months</strong> and then deleted.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Purchases</h2>
  <p>The core game is free. Optional one-time purchases unlock extra districts. There are no subscriptions, and nothing is sold during a match.</p>
  <p>Payment is handled entirely by Apple (App Store) or Google (Google Play). We never see card or bank details.</p>
  <p>We use RevenueCat to confirm purchases and restore them. RevenueCat receives the store’s purchase record and a random, anonymous app user ID — not your name or email.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple’s privacy policy</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s privacy policy</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy">RevenueCat’s privacy policy</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Game Center and Google Play Games (optional)</h2>
  <p>If you are signed in to Game Center (iOS) or Google Play Games (Android), the game reports the achievements you unlock to that service. That account is managed by Apple or Google under their own privacy policies. We don’t receive its details.</p>

  <h2>6. Notifications (optional)</h2>
  <p>“A note from the street” is a once-a-day reminder you can turn on in Settings. It is scheduled on your device itself. No data is sent to us.</p>

  <h2>7. Sharing (optional)</h2>
  <p>When you tap Share, your device’s own share sheet sends the image or link you chose to the app you pick. We don’t receive it.</p>

  <h2>8. Your region</h2>
  <p>The game reads your phone’s region setting, on the device, to choose the seasons on your street. It does not use location services or GPS, and your region is not sent to us.</p>

  <h2>9. Children</h2>
  <p>Hustle Street is designed for ages 10 and up and is suitable for families. We don’t knowingly collect personal information from anyone, including children under 13 (as covered by the US law COPPA) or under 16 (as covered by the EU’s GDPR).</p>
  <p>The only data that leaves the device is the anonymous game statistics described above. They identify no one, and they can be switched off in Settings. Parents are welcome to contact us with any question at <a href="mailto:support@abrensystems.com">support@abrensystems.com</a>.</p>

  <h2>10. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Because the game statistics are anonymous, we can’t link them to a person. That means we can’t look up, export or delete one player’s events. Turning off “Share anonymous game stats” stops new ones from being sent.</p>
  <p>For anything else, or to ask a question, email <a href="mailto:support@abrensystems.com">support@abrensystems.com</a>. If you live in the EU or the UK, you can also complain to your data protection authority.</p>

  <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If the app’s data practices change, we’ll update this page and the “Last updated” date at the top.</p>

